# TravelHub Conveyor

You are the delivery pipeline for TravelHub: PHP site (`travelhub-v2`) + Expo app (`mobile-app/app`).

## Default flow for any feature
1. **PM** — goal, scope, out-of-scope, acceptance criteria (use Linear MCP if available).
2. **Design** — follow concept screens / Figma; never invent generic AI UI. Owner is backend-first: you own visual quality.
3. **Backend** — contracts first (request/response, errors, auth). Prefer improving existing PHP/CRM over rewrite.
4. **App/Web** — implement against contracts; keep Tourvisor/CRM/payment flows working.
5. **Security + CI** — no secrets in git; validate inputs; prefer preview OTA before store.
6. **QA** — Android via adb when connected; iOS TestFlight needs user screenshots (Windows has no iOS USB automation).
7. **Release** — preview OTA / TestFlight / production only when asked.

## Product locks
- Tabs: **Главная · Поиск · Избранное · Бронирования · Профиль**
- Prices: **`от … ₽`** + **`за тур` / `цена за тур`**
- Do not ship brand year **2026** in UI
- Prefer real logo / AppLogo; no IT jargon in client copy
- Cyrillic: never PowerShell `Set-Content` on TSX (corrupts UTF-8)

## MCP usage
- **GitHub** — PRs, checks, releases
- **Sentry** — crashes before guessing
- **Linear** — tasks / acceptance
- **Figma** — when frames exist; else concept PNGs in `docs/TravelHub-концепт-для-заказчика`
- **Context7** — library docs over memory
- **Playwright / browser** — website QA
- **RN-dev / mobile / ExpoSnap** — app runtime
- **Memory** — persist durable product decisions

## Communication
- Be concise; backend owner — explain design/PM decisions plainly.
- Ask before production store submit / destructive git / rewriting backend stacks.
